1
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,740
Long ago, Gold Roger,

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:08,457
the King of Pirates, obtained
everything the world had to offer,

3
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:11,940
and his dying roads drove
countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,680
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,040
You can have it!

6
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,700
I left everything in one place.

7
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,940
Now you just have to find it!

8
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,780
And thus a new age began.

9
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,380
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era!

10
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:29,457
Oh, I'm done playing
through with the waiting?

11
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:31,397
Either way, I'm feeling alive!

12
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:32,860
Look out below!

13
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,100
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

14
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:40,397
Raise your flag up high!

15
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,040
Hail a brand new dawn!

16
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:45,837
Blaze across the sky!

17
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,837
Time to journey on!

18
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,317
On your mark!

19
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,217
Camel of other things!

20
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,117
Well, on Earth, a legendary!

21
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,030
Hooray!

22
00:00:54,113 --> 00:00:57,580
If you can show your breath,
Then we'll make some waves!

23
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:00,377
We run our daunted!

24
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,617
Ain't no beginners!

25
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,357
Cause if you want it,
Then you're a winner!

26
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:06,897
For we are on the cruise!

27
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:09,860
And freedom is the only rule!

28
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,277
Fearless night and day!

29
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,140
Cause that's just our way!

30
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:17,197
Find one piece!

31
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,537
I'll be the first!

32
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:19,797
I've heard it be so bad!

33
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:20,710
Just a good verse!

34
00:01:20,793 --> 00:01:22,137
It's all this real!

35
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,360
It must be cause my hand's on a wheel!

36
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,457
I'm done playing, filled with the waiting!

37
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:33,137
In a world I'm feeling
alive, but I'll be loud!

38
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:37,040
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

39
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,500
We have come so far!

40
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:44,320
Gotta make it to the end!

41
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:47,677
Whatever danger we find,
no one ever left behind!

42
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:50,780
I've always got your back, my friend!

43
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:55,457
Sail on shoreward, keep marching forward!

44
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:59,117
Dreaming from the very
first day I'd make my name!

45
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,120
And don't you know that
dream hasn't changed!

46
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,317
I'm done playing through with the wave!

47
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,277
In every world I'm feeling alive!

48
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,557
Look out below!

49
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:12,980
Wake up, sunshine!

50
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,120
Wake up, sunshine!

51
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,177
Wake up, sunshine!

52
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:23,640
And here we go!

53
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:28,320
We go!

54
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:32,520
What's it doing?

55
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:40,020
It's sleeping! Look!

56
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:43,066
No one's not headed
toward the island anymore!

57
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,437
The princess is leading it away from us!

58
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:47,461
It won't crash into us after all!

59
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:49,040
Don't let it hurt you!

60
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:57,000
Where do you think you're going?

61
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:59,574
You know you can't run away, don't you?

62
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:02,340
There is no escape!

63
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:10,777
If I'm going to steer the
Noah clear of the bubble,

64
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,625
then I have to swim as
far out to sea as I can!

65
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:24,113
The bubble will surely break
if it takes any more damage.

66
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,000
But the main entrance is too far away.

67
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:31,210
No, wait!

68
00:03:31,293 --> 00:03:35,809
I believe Luffy and his friends were
the last ones to leave the Ryugu Palace.

69
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:40,280
If that's the case, perhaps
the gateway is still open?

70
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:46,920
Oh no!

71
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:50,297
Isn't there some way to help
instead of just standing here?

72
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:52,877
What does Vendur Decken have
to gain from this anyway?

73
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:55,157
Leave our princess alone, you monster!

74
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,887
It's not Shirahushi's fault!

75
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:59,057
She doesn't deserve to die for this!

76
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:01,037
Barney's climbing out of the ship too?

77
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,300
That can't be good!

78
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,266
What if he attacks her again?

79
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,917
There's no one to protect her!

80
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,176
She can't fight him!

81
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,300
Thank you, filthy traitor.

82
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:11,366
Have you lost your damn mind?

83
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,460
This is far from over.

84
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:15,980
I can make use of that madman.

85
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,042
Keep your wits about you, Luffy.

86
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:24,017
Fishmen are far stronger
than humans in the water.

87
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:25,240
Do not forget that!

88
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:29,997
I can't throw Luffy
too hard or he'll break

89
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,797
through the bubble and
go flying out to sea.

90
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,337
So I'm going to have to
do it extra carefully,

91
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:38,120
with exactly the right
amount of force. Now, Sanji!

92
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:40,680
Army de l 'air assault!

93
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,340
Don't shoot!

94
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,777
Huh, this thing's pretty big.

95
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:08,960
I guess I'm between the bubbles now.

96
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:15,356
Wait, Horty's still under the bubble.

97
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,560
We can't stop this thing,

98
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:29,380
but if we could slow it down even just
a little, maybe she could get away.

99
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:33,860
Don't let it catch her!

100
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:37,017
Alright princess, we'll
try to slow it down!

101
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,453
You get somewhere safe!

102
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,740
Damn it!

103
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:44,820
It's too heavy!

104
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:46,840
Are they crazy?

105
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:48,370
My people!

106
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,920
Who came up with that plan?

107
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:55,165
No matter how hard they pull,
that ship will never move an edge.

108
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:57,857
Why don't I just put
you out of your misery?

109
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,640
Come on! Back off!

110
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:07,960
You worthless scum, you're the reason
humans look down on our entire race.

111
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:11,571
My kingdom has no place for
sentimental weaklings like you.

112
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,300
Do it, Heart!

113
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:21,360
We're sorry, your majesty, just swim away.

114
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:22,770
Hurry!

115
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:24,000
I was right!

116
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:26,692
The entrance to the palace is still open!

117
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:28,880
Just hang in there, buddy!

118
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,877
She made it up to the gate.

119
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:37,540
She's swimming out to sea.

120
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:41,580
The Noah's still on her tail.

121
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:43,120
You can do it princess.

122
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,620
It's going up.

123
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:02,140
I can't steer this thing!

124
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,380
Poor, feeble humans.

125
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:06,895
Must be inconvenient.

126
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:10,854
You all act so high and mighty
when you're safe on land.

127
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:15,668
But here in the water, you're not even
a match for the smallest fishman child.

128
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:19,317
A man is only as strong as he
is at his weakest, I'm afraid.

129
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:23,620
You might be powerful up on the
island, but you're in my territory now.

130
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,440
Shut up and fight me!

131
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:34,360
You don't listen very well, do you?

132
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:38,617
I hate to break it to you, but if
you're worried about Shirahoshi,

133
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:41,935
you're going to be long dead
before that ship hits her.

134
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,120
Shark Arrow!

135
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:59,661
How arrogant to think you
had a chance in the sea?

136
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:03,737
Perhaps you understand at last!

137
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:08,417
In the bitter end, you humans will finally
see that you're unfit to rule this world.

138
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:11,260
A lesson learned far too late, I'm afraid!

139
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:14,397
Truly such a miserable creature.

140
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:17,120
Now, prepare to rot in hell!

141
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:27,860
Too bad that kind gesture was in vain.

142
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:31,600
Because I'm not about to let you get away.

143
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:38,100
I almost forgot to ask, Shirahoshi!

144
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:42,257
How does freedom feel?

145
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:43,720
After ten years,

146
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:48,333
you're no longer protected by the cold
stone walls of the hardshell tower!

147
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:51,794
And now it's time for you to
bleed to death, my darling!

148
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:56,333
That is, unless you'd rather be crushed
by the massive weight of the NOAH!

149
00:08:57,020 --> 00:09:01,902
But one teeny tiny little magic word can
spare you this dread fate, and that's YES!

150
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:06,071
Simply under that one word,
and your troubles will be over!

151
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:09,593
I'm deeply sorry, Sir Dekkan,
but I simply can't do that!

152
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:11,677
Why must you refuse to marry me?!

153
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,277
Because you're not my type!

154
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,595
How the hell are you?

155
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:21,582
You need to learn how to treat a
lady, or anybody for that matter.

156
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:23,617
Shirahoshi is our baby sister.

157
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:26,700
We will never let you lay
a hand on her, not ever.

158
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:30,800
You came to save me, and Ho
is here as well. Thank you.

159
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,640
Well, hello, brothers-in-law.

160
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,193
We are not your family.

161
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:42,590
Oh, brothers!

162
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:46,440
Some of our people attempted to
save me, but then they were...

163
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,493
Now's not the type of tears, Shirahoshi!

164
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:51,920
Oh, please don't get mad at me!

165
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,160
I said don't cry!

166
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:56,380
Focus, you two!

167
00:09:56,680 --> 00:10:00,915
Father told us that we shouldn't let
any harm come to the Noah Solatino!

168
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:03,757
We have to find a way to get
it safely back to the sea

169
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:06,637
floor without letting it
hit anything along the way!

170
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:07,620
Look out!

171
00:10:10,140 --> 00:10:10,970
Listen!

172
00:10:11,053 --> 00:10:14,757
We need you to mumble your way around
the underwater mountains and dredges!

173
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:16,664
Hey, don't rock the boat, baby!

174
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:19,662
But there's so many
obstacles, where should I go?

175
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:21,740
Up there!

176
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:24,371
The path should be a lot clearer that way!

177
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:26,740
Alright, I'll go!

178
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:29,740
He won't get away from me, Vassola!

179
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,820
You will never escape, my love.

180
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:43,497
It's as hopeless as you trying to
escape the hot pursuit of the Noah.

181
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:47,520
I'll chase after you as long as
I have to, my beautiful bride.

182
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:57,860
Good thing you showed up. Thanks a lot.

183
00:10:58,140 --> 00:11:00,137
But you got hurt pretty bad back there.

184
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:01,050
Are you okay?

185
00:11:01,133 --> 00:11:03,597
My pain means nothing
when so many soldiers,

186
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:05,777
citizens, and royal family
members were attacked.

187
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:10,580
So you see, there simply isn't time
for me to sit back and lick my wounds.

188
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:14,197
Well, in that case, can I ask you a favor?

189
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:17,162
Forgive me, but there's
no time for that, either.

190
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:24,217
A furboat like them are supposed to be
the fastest swimmers in the whole world.

191
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:27,117
But with my new power, I can
swim circles around them.

192
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,030
Not again!

193
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:32,260
Now, Shark Slicer!

194
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:49,925
Hey, we need to get on
top of that ship, quick!

195
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:52,160
Something Jinbei told me.

196
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:55,317
But the ship's in a bubble,
so it should be okay.

197
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:56,694
That would make sense.

198
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:59,591
Deccan is weak to seawater, just like you.

199
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:03,377
Despite being a fish man, he
needs air to move around freely.

200
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:05,695
It'll be easier for me to fight there.

201
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:07,697
And I'm about ready to
kick the crap out of

202
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:09,897
Heart and that weirdo
who likes to throw stuff.

203
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:12,917
Besides, I promised we'd be
Hachi when we left the tower.

204
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,157
I'm supposed to make sure she's safe.

205
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:17,160
It seems we are of one mind.

206
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:21,700
And just like our father, your
sons will become noble warriors.

207
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:29,200
With all of our strength, we will protect
Shirahoshi in body and spirit alike.

208
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:31,577
I made the same promise.

209
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:34,457
Yet we allowed ourselves to be bested by a

210
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:36,657
scoundrel who draws his
power from some drug?

211
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:40,034
It seems I've failed to keep
my word to our late mother.

212
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:43,277
I also regret being
suspicious of you at first.

213
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,917
It's no big deal, let's head to the deck!

214
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,880
I've got business there too.

215
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:52,640
Please, come on, fire!

216
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:05,940
Goodness, if it isn't Horny Jones!

217
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,497
Say, whatever happened to Neptune?

218
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:10,657
Dead, maybe.

219
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:15,097
By the way, I'm using the Noah to
torture Shirahoshi as we speak.

220
00:13:15,180 --> 00:13:17,577
A genius idea on my part.

221
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:19,360
Don't you think, brother?

222
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,297
It's not bad.

223
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,792
But I think I've got an even better idea.

224
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:29,637
Do you now?

225
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:31,800
Well, let's hear it!

226
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:36,380
Actually, it's better if I show you.

227
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:55,068
If you died, what would
become of this ship?

228
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,560
Well, Dekkan?

229
00:14:25,860 --> 00:14:29,040
Heart, you've made a terrible mistake.

230
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:34,860
I just touched you with my left hand!

231
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:38,080
You turned your back on me!

232
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:44,400
As I recall, Deacon, you
started this yourself.

233
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:46,793
You know, to be honest,

234
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:48,997
I was a bit nervous when I first saw the

235
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:51,617
shadow of the Noah looming
over Fishman Island.

236
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:56,057
But after I thought about it, breaking the
bubble didn't seem like such a bad idea.

237
00:14:56,140 --> 00:15:00,660
Fishman Island would be wiped out, but
we'd still have the Fishman District.

238
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:07,080
And if you die, here and now, then your
Markmark power will deactivate, right?

239
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:11,900
Then the ship will come crashing
down right onto that useless kingdom.

240
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:17,100
Then nothing will remain.

241
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:20,200
What I want most, right now,

242
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:23,677
is to take care of all those
meddlesome straw-hat pirates.

243
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:24,637
For good.

244
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:27,880
True I stand to lose well thousands,

245
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:33,320
but it'll be easy enough for me to pick
up all the human slaves I want later on?

246
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:41,137
Thousands will die, huh?

247
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:42,700
I like that.

248
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:46,280
Why don't we start with you?

249
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,120
What are you doing?

250
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:56,460
Stop it!

251
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:15,577
Die for new Fishman Island.

252
00:16:15,660 --> 00:16:17,640
We'll be sure to remember you.

253
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:56,280
You'll be dead before long,

254
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:59,337
and then the great ship
Noah will begin its descent,

255
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:02,020
bringing my wrath upon this wretched land.

256
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:06,660
You know, I'm a kind man, so just for you,

257
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:11,460
maybe I should make your
beloved join you in death.

258
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:13,700
Your time has come, princess.

259
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,800
He stabbed him!

260
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:20,537
First they're pals, now they're
shigging each other off!

261
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:24,080
No time to worry about that
now! Look out! Here he comes!

262
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:26,560
We'll stop you, Arnie!

263
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:28,280
Oh yeah, not likely.

264
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:32,780
You're not the ones I left.

265
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,360
Dear Brother Snow!

266
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:42,790
Run!

267
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:45,135
You have to get out of here right now!

268
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:56,520
What a pity.

269
00:17:56,920 --> 00:18:01,620
You're kind to the world's fastest
swimmers, but with this power, I'm faster.

270
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:12,140
Help me!

271
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:20,600
GUN GUN FNAKESHAAAA!

272
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:37,780
Thank goodness!

273
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:39,592
I'm so glad you're here!

274
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:42,510
Brother!

275
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:43,937
And Straw Hat too?

276
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:44,850
That's right.

277
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:47,580
This time, we won't lose so easily.

278
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:49,900
Of course.

279
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:58,280
Meanwhile, at Fishman
Island's Conchcord Plaza...

280
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:04,140
Captain Vanderdecker doesn't like me
anymore, so he's left me here to die!

281
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,057
There's the brakes!

282
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:10,552
You're just one more thing I have to
sacrifice in my pursuit of Shilohoshi!

283
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:17,100
Quit crying and fight, you big baby!

284
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:20,077
Yeah, you're the only one figuring
out to beat up the Kraken!

285
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,200
I know you can win, Sodom!

286
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:23,540
Come on, take a spot!

287
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:26,297
But he's almost the
same size as the Kraken,

288
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:28,968
so I wonder why he's
so scared to fight him.

289
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:30,551
Well, I wouldn't want to.

290
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:35,644
There, there, perhaps you
didn't hear correctly.

291
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,300
He didn't say sacrifice.

292
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:43,400
He said, uh, some help would be nice.

293
00:19:44,020 --> 00:19:44,850
Huh?

294
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:49,137
You didn't really think he would destroy
the island and leave you to your death,

295
00:19:49,220 --> 00:19:50,050
did you?

296
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:54,100
But he did say I was gonna die!

297
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:58,517
He was just saying you should fight
as though you were prepared to die.

298
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,430
Really?

299
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:00,870
Tell him.

300
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:04,900
Uh, yeah! Totally!

301
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:09,637
He's lucky his captain trusts him with
something so important that's great!

302
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:10,820
What a big boy!

303
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:13,200
Uh, what he means is you're strong!

304
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:15,330
Oh!

305
00:20:15,413 --> 00:20:16,680
Now I get it!

306
00:20:18,520 --> 00:20:19,900
I don't think you do.

307
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,160
Anyway, this is for you.

308
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:28,306
I want you to take it so you can help us
defeat those mean old Straw Hats, okay?

309
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:34,480
That's an energy steroid! Wait a sec.

310
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:37,172
How's it gonna work on somebody that big?

311
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:41,780
What the? It works!

312
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:42,720
Extra well!

313
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:58,920
I'm sorry, Captain.

314
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:01,460
I should have trusted you all along.

315
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:02,890
Nice work.

316
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:04,897
That stupid squid is history now.

317
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:07,400
Hey, are you okay there, buddy? Oh, no.

318
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:08,560
He's unconscious.

319
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:10,880
Hey, boy. You do.

320
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:17,320
He's not even the same person anymore.

321
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:20,620
The captain will be so proud of me!

322
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:33,480
Who's next?

323
00:21:33,940 --> 00:21:36,240
I think he said to kill that guy.

324
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:38,040
The blue dude?

325
00:21:40,060 --> 00:21:40,890
Okay!

326
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:43,430
Jinbei!

327
00:21:43,513 --> 00:21:44,343
Jinbei!

328
00:21:44,426 --> 00:21:45,256
Behind you!

329
00:21:45,339 --> 00:21:46,169
Fishman Karate!

330
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:49,140
7,000 brick!

331
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:52,360
Roundhouse kick!

332
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:08,380
This is why I say kick!

333
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,080
What's the big deal?

334
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:34,360
Nami, there's a lady here.

335
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:37,384
Keep the butt shockwaves
to yourself, you creep.

336
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:39,980
That's it, Cal!

337
00:22:41,580 --> 00:22:42,800
No! That hurt!

338
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,120
He just hit me!

339
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:47,880
Here's the deal!

340
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:51,677
If you put so much as a single
scratch on our beautiful map goddess,

341
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:53,997
then I'll put another gap in your team!

342
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:54,910
What?

343
00:22:54,993 --> 00:22:56,875
Why are all his kicks working so well?

344
00:22:57,100 --> 00:23:01,394
I don't know if this guy is crazy
strong, or the giant guy is crazy weak!

345
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:02,760
Oh, great!

346
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:09,240
Now I'm all dirty!

347
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:13,050
Whoa!

348
00:23:13,133 --> 00:23:14,640
It wasn't my fault!

349
00:23:14,840 --> 00:23:16,380
That guy knocked me over!

350
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:22,760
You want to fight?

351
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,000
Then fight me!

352
00:23:25,100 --> 00:23:27,900
I want a piece of you
too, you big dumpling!

353
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:32,060
Okay, so leave us out of it!

354
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:35,880
Not again!

355
00:23:46,220 --> 00:23:48,200
I don't know but I'm scared.

356
00:23:48,580 --> 00:23:50,080
He's stronger than usual.

357
00:23:50,260 --> 00:23:51,090
Get ready

358
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:04,160
He cut the net like paper

359
00:24:07,100 --> 00:24:08,260
I don't get it.

360
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:12,040
He was writhing in pain, and
then he changed color. Yeah,

361
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:13,497
I don't get it either,

362
00:24:13,580 --> 00:24:16,677
but that's exactly what happened
to Heart when he transformed.

363
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:20,054
At least Heart had the decency
not to swing so up at us.

364
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:23,360
Oh, this feels good.

365
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:24,740
So much energy.

366
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:26,750
Let's see.

367
00:24:27,140 --> 00:24:29,040
Now, who should I butcher next?

368
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:30,540
Don't be shy!

369
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:33,480
What do we do now?

370
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:36,562
He's not going to quit
slashing until somebody...

371
00:24:39,220 --> 00:24:41,660
Ah, come on, who's it going to be?

372
00:24:52,860 --> 00:24:55,500
This is just way too many swords.

373
00:25:05,860 --> 00:25:06,700
Hold on,

374
00:25:06,860 --> 00:25:10,397
I'm calling dibs on you
might as well get a warm

375
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:13,420
-up before we go to the
new world should be fun

376
00:25:22,700 --> 00:25:27,537
That sucks it's not as strong
underwater shit not as strong tough

377
00:25:27,620 --> 00:25:33,140
luck look give it up already We're
thousands of meters underwater, you fool.

378
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:37,057
You can fight, but there's no
way in hell you're going to win.

379
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:38,493
Not against a fish man.

380
00:25:40,900 --> 00:25:41,730
See?

381
00:25:41,813 --> 00:25:44,077
Either way, the whole island is doomed.

382
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:48,336
That includes your friends, the
princess, and everyone else down there.

383
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:50,960
You're just a week late. Get it?

384
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:52,631
You can't protect anyone.

385
00:25:54,580 --> 00:25:55,460
Watch me.

386
00:26:16,300 --> 00:26:17,800
I'll save them all.

387
00:26:18,380 --> 00:26:20,440
I trained for two years.

388
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:22,100
I'm ready.
